ic place and obviously  we're all going to make jokes about  where he went and where he ended up but  any public place is to me an egregious  violation i mean  the bubble has started you are in you're  on an excused absence  to attend a family funeral does it  really need to be explained that the  only place you should go  is that family funeral and get back on  get back on a plane and get back to this  bubble  as quickly as possible i mean it i i  really don't think that needed to be  spelled out i mean it is  it was irresponsible it was selfish  and you know thank god it was  photographed because  you know he could have gotten back here  and no one would have known where he was  and and that would have been 10 times  worse but the reality is  the nba has limitations in in how it can  sanction him  and so rishon holmes and lou williams  get the same  10-day back in quarantine basically  because that's what the league has  collectively bargained with the union on  these matters  you know everybody's saying why why are  the punishments the same well that's why  the nba  really didn't have much of an option  assess the clippers situation  uh from a basketball perspective that we  came into  the bubble and they were as deep as any  team in the nba  and a lot of people like them to emerge  from the western conference here but  how would you handicap them i mean joe  kim noah  is their center i mean well here's the  thing they do have time  i mean seedings matter  nothing in terms of home court advantage  they matter  as far as who you might play so  obviously they don't want to fall too  far down the ladder because you don't  want to make your road  unnecessarily tougher having to play  tougher teams but  they do have time that you know all  these teams are playing eight games  before we even get to the playoffs so  yeah i mean  it doesn't look great right now when you  have no harold  no lou williams pat beverly just got  back no zubach i mean they're missing  they're 